WEBVTT

00:48.089 --> 00:49.257
Thanks for the food.

01:12.113 --> 01:13.490
You're that guy from the last game.

01:36.554 --> 01:37.472
Do you want to live?

01:51.820 --> 01:52.654
I…

01:54.823 --> 01:55.907
I'll die too.

01:58.827 --> 01:59.661
Is that so?

02:01.621 --> 02:02.622
I got it.

02:37.824 --> 02:38.908
Thanks for the food.

03:12.942 --> 03:14.777
LIFE IN THE WOODS BY HENRY DAVID THOREAU

05:01.217 --> 05:02.885
It's so beautiful.

05:05.054 --> 05:05.888
Yes.

05:08.933 --> 05:10.018
Father.

05:12.770 --> 05:14.564
If God exists,

05:15.773 --> 05:17.150
what would you wish for?

05:27.744 --> 05:30.580
Please create more mountains
around the world!

05:30.663 --> 05:33.041
Mountains that no one has ever climbed.

05:33.124 --> 05:34.042
Please!

05:38.087 --> 05:39.130
You're so strange!

05:41.424 --> 05:45.511
I don't think there are any mountains
that have not been climbed by humans.

05:47.305 --> 05:48.139
And you, Yuzuha?

05:53.978 --> 05:56.481
Please let things stay like this forever!

06:03.529 --> 06:04.572
Mountains.

06:05.948 --> 06:07.158
They are the only place…

06:09.243 --> 06:12.163
where I'm accepted as I am.

06:14.332 --> 06:20.129
And you are the only one
who accepts me as I am, Father.

06:25.468 --> 06:27.762
I just want things
to stay like this forever.

06:32.350 --> 06:33.351
You're so strange.

06:49.700 --> 06:50.701
That's his daughter!

06:50.785 --> 06:53.496
- Ms. Usagi?
- Excuse me!

06:53.579 --> 06:55.832
Can we please have a word with you?

06:55.915 --> 06:56.916
There are claims

06:56.999 --> 06:59.752
that his solo no-oxygen climb
on the Southwest route was staged.

06:59.836 --> 07:03.881
- Your response, please!
- Have you heard anything from your father?

07:03.965 --> 07:06.134
- Ms. Yuzuha Usagi?
- Ms. Usagi?

07:08.010 --> 07:08.886
Welcome home.

07:12.348 --> 07:13.266
Father.

07:14.684 --> 07:18.396
I don't know who came up with
that sham article,

07:19.897 --> 07:21.566
but I never lie.

07:29.323 --> 07:30.741
Where are you going?

07:31.742 --> 07:32.827
The mountains.

07:48.342 --> 07:49.343
Father?

07:53.806 --> 07:54.682
The mountains.

07:55.850 --> 07:58.186
They accept me for who I am.

08:11.282 --> 08:14.035
- Mr. Usagi?
- You're Shigenori Usagi, right?

08:23.586 --> 08:27.089
STAGED?!

08:27.173 --> 08:30.092
SOLO NO-OXYGEN MOUNTAIN CLIMBING
SUSPECTED TO BE STAGED

08:30.176 --> 08:32.595
HE USED AN OXYGEN TANK

08:32.678 --> 08:35.598
IT WAS AN IMPOSSIBLE CHALLENGE
IN THE FIRST PLACE

08:35.681 --> 08:38.976
DID USAGI STAGE THE ENTIRE EVENT?

08:39.060 --> 08:42.104
550-STRONG SEARCH PARTY
LOOK FOR MISSING CLIMBER

08:42.188 --> 08:48.861
NO CLUES ON HIS WHEREABOUTS

08:48.945 --> 08:51.405
WORLD-FAMOUS MOUNTAINEER MISSING

08:51.489 --> 08:55.117
SHINEGORI USAGI COMMITS SUICIDE
FOLLOWING RUMORS OF STAGED CLIMB?

08:55.201 --> 08:58.829
SUICIDE

10:02.351 --> 10:03.728
Thanks for the food.

10:17.408 --> 10:18.784
Why did you save me?

10:31.130 --> 10:33.257
Your body is saying that it wants to live.

10:36.177 --> 10:37.345
My body?

10:41.390 --> 10:43.059
My body wants to live…

10:49.732 --> 10:52.234
But there's no point in me living.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.033
Everyone died.

11:02.578 --> 11:04.789
Because I was the only one who survived.

11:08.292 --> 11:11.128
Everyone died because I survived.

11:15.633 --> 11:18.260
I was the one who killed all of them.

11:21.138 --> 11:23.516
I killed them!

11:26.477 --> 11:28.312
Someone like me…

11:29.605 --> 11:32.024
It's unforgivable
for someone like me to be alive!

11:35.111 --> 11:36.529
I'll die.

11:38.656 --> 11:39.865
I'll die.

11:41.409 --> 11:42.827
I'll die!

11:45.037 --> 11:47.289
I'll die and go to them.

11:49.041 --> 11:53.504
I have to kneel and apologize to them!

11:54.714 --> 11:58.092
I have to apologize to them right now!

12:08.519 --> 12:09.645
Even so.

12:12.523 --> 12:13.691
Why?

12:20.698 --> 12:21.699
My body.

12:25.453 --> 12:26.787
It's saying that it's hungry.

12:33.461 --> 12:37.965
There have been times
I've wanted to die, too.

12:43.345 --> 12:44.555
But I'm the same as you.

12:47.391 --> 12:48.976
I laid down for so long

12:50.936 --> 12:52.938
that my stomach started getting hungry.

12:59.403 --> 13:01.113
I'm going to die anyway.

13:04.992 --> 13:07.787
I might die during tomorrow's game,

13:08.454 --> 13:10.164
or I might die when my visa expires.

13:17.505 --> 13:19.298
I made the effort to cook that for you,

13:21.175 --> 13:22.968
so you should eat it before you die.

14:50.556 --> 14:51.557
Get ready.

14:56.228 --> 14:57.479
You're joining the game, right?

15:03.527 --> 15:05.821
Are you planning to die
by letting your visa expire?

15:18.500 --> 15:20.336
Why did you scream at that time?

15:27.551 --> 15:28.636
During the tag game.

15:32.389 --> 15:35.225
You tried to save everyone
even at the cost of your life.

15:35.935 --> 15:36.810
- Everyone!
- Hey!

15:36.894 --> 15:39.772
The tagger is currently
on the second level of the central area!

15:39.855 --> 15:42.024
Let's inform each other
of the tagger's location

15:42.107 --> 15:44.026
and search for the safezone together!

15:49.448 --> 15:50.950
That's because I didn't want to die.

15:57.206 --> 15:59.708
I didn't want everyone to die.

16:04.254 --> 16:05.673
I'm the same.

16:07.424 --> 16:09.259
I don't want you to die.

16:12.930 --> 16:16.475
If you hadn't shouted, I would have died.

16:27.569 --> 16:28.821
Let me return the favor.

17:06.775 --> 17:08.902
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

18:53.841 --> 18:55.384
ONE PER PERSON

19:06.270 --> 19:08.397
FACIAL RECOGNITION IN PROGRESS
PLEASE WAIT A MOMENT

19:10.691 --> 19:12.067
You guys aren't new to this.

19:14.695 --> 19:15.863
What about you guys?

19:17.281 --> 19:19.241
The three of us
cleared four games together.

19:20.409 --> 19:22.119
We happened to be together
in our first game,

19:22.202 --> 19:23.829
and we stuck together after that.

19:24.788 --> 19:28.417
Having friends makes the difference
between winning and losing.

19:31.211 --> 19:33.130
Your leg. Are you injured?

19:35.883 --> 19:36.717
Yes,

19:37.843 --> 19:38.927
I guess I sprained it.

19:40.262 --> 19:41.430
During a game?

19:44.016 --> 19:45.601
Well, yes.

19:50.731 --> 19:52.316
Hey, it's starting.

19:53.025 --> 19:55.235
Registration has closed.

19:55.319 --> 19:57.362
The game will now commence.

19:58.197 --> 20:00.741
Difficulty, Four of Clubs.

20:02.701 --> 20:03.702
Distance.

20:05.204 --> 20:06.330
Distance.

20:06.955 --> 20:12.794
Rule. Endure the trial
and reach the goal within the time limit.

20:13.670 --> 20:17.424
Clear condition. Reach the goal safely.

20:18.508 --> 20:19.593
What's this?

20:19.676 --> 20:21.345
Game start.

20:22.429 --> 20:24.973
One hundred twenty minutes remaining.

20:27.935 --> 20:29.228
Are they asking us to run?

20:31.146 --> 20:32.481
What do you think, Seizan?

20:37.861 --> 20:38.695
Distance?

20:41.740 --> 20:44.201
Are we supposed
to run on a highway or something?

20:46.495 --> 20:48.247
Run? Oh, no…

20:48.330 --> 20:50.540
Takuma. It will be fine.

20:52.084 --> 20:53.085
Sit there.

20:53.961 --> 20:56.797
This bus has a carburetor model
from the early 1970s.

21:00.342 --> 21:02.803
If I can just get the engine started…

21:08.225 --> 21:09.935
Damn it, no gas!

21:11.311 --> 21:13.355
Then I guess we have no choice but to run.

21:19.611 --> 21:20.737
Leave me.

21:28.620 --> 21:29.454
Takuma!

21:29.538 --> 21:30.706
I'm not saying

21:31.581 --> 21:34.501
that I'll sacrifice myself and die here!

21:36.962 --> 21:39.006
I'll search for a way for me to survive,

21:40.841 --> 21:41.925
so you guys go ahead.

21:46.346 --> 21:48.974
- There's no way we can do that!
- Yamane!

21:50.976 --> 21:53.228
You have to clear the game!

21:54.354 --> 21:56.356
You want to see your wife again, right?

21:57.399 --> 21:59.401
And the baby in her belly!

22:01.820 --> 22:04.323
If you die,
what's going to happen to your family?

22:11.288 --> 22:12.789
Don't mind me.

22:13.457 --> 22:14.791
I'll figure something out.

22:23.633 --> 22:24.551
Yamane.

22:26.595 --> 22:27.679
Let's go.

22:32.893 --> 22:33.935
Go.

22:35.896 --> 22:36.772
Please.

22:37.689 --> 22:38.857
It was fun with you guys.

22:48.658 --> 22:49.785
Let's go.

22:58.543 --> 22:59.461
We should go.

23:10.263 --> 23:11.890
It's the right thing to do.

23:22.567 --> 23:25.112
One hundred ten minutes remaining.

23:50.887 --> 23:52.055
Arisu.

23:52.139 --> 23:53.306
Live on for us.

23:53.890 --> 23:55.142
Thank you.

24:23.462 --> 24:25.088
Distance, 1,000.

24:35.932 --> 24:37.809
Ninety minutes remaining.

24:39.227 --> 24:43.398
They told us to reach the goal,
but how much further do we need to run?

24:56.786 --> 24:58.497
Distance, 5,000.

25:07.339 --> 25:08.423
What's over there?

25:14.971 --> 25:16.890
REPLENISHMENT STATION

25:22.145 --> 25:23.563
What a lifesaver.

25:31.738 --> 25:33.907
Wait. Are you going to drink it?

25:37.619 --> 25:39.204
Is this a test for us?

25:42.582 --> 25:43.833
How can that be?

25:52.551 --> 25:53.593
Take this.

25:54.761 --> 25:56.054
Thanks.

26:07.816 --> 26:08.984
I feel so alive now.

26:17.617 --> 26:18.743
Is that fine?

26:19.744 --> 26:20.620
Yes.

26:39.973 --> 26:41.766
Distance, 6,000.

26:43.768 --> 26:46.813
This place is kind of dark.

26:53.570 --> 26:57.949
This is tough. This is more like
a Spades game than a Clubs game.

27:01.578 --> 27:02.746
Something's there.

27:11.046 --> 27:12.255
There's nothing.

27:12.839 --> 27:14.716
No. Something's there.

27:32.942 --> 27:33.943
Arisu.

28:58.069 --> 28:58.945
Damn it!

29:15.211 --> 29:16.087
Run!

29:25.054 --> 29:28.767
Shit. This is seriously bad!

29:36.733 --> 29:37.984
Go!

29:39.235 --> 29:41.529
Just go!

29:42.155 --> 29:43.281
Seizan!

29:43.364 --> 29:45.617
- Let's go!
- Seizan!

29:46.201 --> 29:48.578
Seizan!

29:48.661 --> 29:51.289
Seizan!

29:55.752 --> 29:57.086
I can't run any further.

29:57.587 --> 29:58.546
You can do it!

30:02.300 --> 30:03.218
I'm…

30:06.805 --> 30:07.680
all alone now.

30:14.187 --> 30:17.982
I was only with them for a week.

30:21.361 --> 30:22.737
But it felt as if…

30:24.697 --> 30:26.533
we had been friends for a long time.

30:35.041 --> 30:38.670
Live on and talk about them
with your wife.

30:49.597 --> 30:50.431
You're right.

31:04.904 --> 31:06.739
Distance, 8,000.

31:21.963 --> 31:22.881
What's the matter?

31:24.048 --> 31:25.049
This motorcycle.

31:27.969 --> 31:29.345
It's a Royal Enfield.

31:31.472 --> 31:32.557
You know your stuff.

31:34.517 --> 31:36.603
It's a rare motorcycle
that uses a diesel engine.

31:40.773 --> 31:43.151
But things like this still work, huh?

31:43.234 --> 31:46.404
Since they don't have IC chips installed.

31:48.656 --> 31:49.657
I see.

31:50.450 --> 31:51.910
It's the electrical circuits.

31:53.328 --> 31:55.997
All the electrical circuits
around this area have been destroyed.

31:57.040 --> 31:57.874
So what?

31:57.957 --> 32:01.002
So in contrast, analog equipment
can be operated here.

32:01.085 --> 32:03.338
It means old motorcycles or cars
may work here.

32:03.421 --> 32:06.341
Whether it's this motorcycle
or the bus at the starting point!

32:11.137 --> 32:12.597
But there are no batteries.

32:15.016 --> 32:18.019
You said this motorcycle is a rare model
that uses a diesel engine, right?

32:18.102 --> 32:19.145
Yes.

32:19.228 --> 32:21.606
So it runs on diesel fuel
instead of gasoline.

32:22.190 --> 32:23.733
That bus runs on diesel too!

32:26.611 --> 32:29.572
So we have to carry this all the way
back to the starting point?

32:30.156 --> 32:33.326
If we transport the fuel back there,
we can save him.

32:33.910 --> 32:35.912
Are you saying that you'll save Takuma?

32:35.995 --> 32:36.996
But if you go,

32:37.497 --> 32:39.248
you can't clear the game!

32:39.332 --> 32:40.375
There's still time.

32:40.458 --> 32:42.377
We still have half the duration left.

32:42.460 --> 32:44.712
Usagi, you head to the goal with him!

32:44.796 --> 32:47.757
I'll be right behind. If the bus moves,
we'll reach the goal easily.

32:49.050 --> 32:51.302
Letting someone die so I can survive…

32:52.261 --> 32:53.638
I'll never do that again.

33:14.701 --> 33:16.953
Distance, 7,000.

33:23.626 --> 33:25.420
Distance, 10,000.

33:41.227 --> 33:43.438
Distance, 12,000.

33:49.861 --> 33:51.612
Distance, 4,000.

34:05.001 --> 34:06.002
What?

34:08.546 --> 34:09.505
Is that the goal?

34:13.009 --> 34:15.219
So we'll wait for them here?

34:24.979 --> 34:26.731
Distance, 1,000.

34:32.195 --> 34:34.822
Fifteen minutes remaining.

34:37.366 --> 34:38.534
Hey!

34:46.959 --> 34:48.086
Hey!

34:57.261 --> 34:58.387
Hey!

35:11.943 --> 35:15.655
ENTRY PROHIBITED

35:24.247 --> 35:25.164
Is that your wife?

35:32.380 --> 35:35.383
The baby's supposed to be due in autumn.

35:45.852 --> 35:47.979
I'm sure they must be safe somewhere.

35:53.776 --> 35:54.902
I'm sure of it.

35:57.530 --> 35:58.406
Everyone.

36:02.285 --> 36:03.995
They should all be safe somewhere.

36:08.749 --> 36:10.334
They didn't just disappear into thin air.

36:18.926 --> 36:20.636
So we have to survive and go back.

36:34.108 --> 36:35.943
Five minutes remaining.

36:36.694 --> 36:38.404
I wonder if they can make it here.

36:45.578 --> 36:46.662
What was that?

36:51.667 --> 36:52.543
What was that?

37:02.720 --> 37:03.638
Water?

37:54.981 --> 37:56.190
I can't run anymore!

37:56.274 --> 37:58.567
You have to run! Don't look back!

38:10.037 --> 38:11.205
Damn it!

38:27.722 --> 38:28.806
Usagi!

38:36.272 --> 38:37.356
Arisu!

39:25.529 --> 39:26.655
Arisu.

39:49.720 --> 39:50.638
It hurts.

39:54.642 --> 39:55.768
Is everyone all right?

40:10.783 --> 40:12.827
Thanks.

40:37.893 --> 40:39.478
I was always…

40:41.856 --> 40:43.232
right inside the goal?

40:46.819 --> 40:48.946
It was written there right from the start.

40:49.697 --> 40:51.323
This was the goal.

40:53.701 --> 40:55.953
So what did those numbers mean?

40:56.662 --> 40:57.913
Distance from the goal.

40:59.457 --> 41:01.041
It should have been zero.

41:10.176 --> 41:11.469
Game cleared.

41:12.178 --> 41:13.554
Congratulations.

41:19.226 --> 41:20.394
Are you all right?

41:21.854 --> 41:23.105
Thanks.

41:34.867 --> 41:35.993
Where are you going?

41:43.292 --> 41:44.210
Who knows?

41:46.462 --> 41:47.796
I don't know myself.

41:56.263 --> 41:57.765
If we're still alive…

42:01.602 --> 42:02.978
let's meet somewhere, okay?

42:33.801 --> 42:34.718
The Beach?

42:36.345 --> 42:38.222
Maybe the people
who disappeared are there.

42:40.307 --> 42:41.976
Could it be
some sort of evacuation shelter?

42:42.601 --> 42:43.727
I don't know.

42:45.479 --> 42:47.147
But I'm sure we'll find our answer there.

42:49.692 --> 42:51.860
I want to believe in what Karube said.

42:54.113 --> 42:55.447
I'll avenge everyone.

42:57.241 --> 42:59.785
I'll stop the mastermind of this game

43:00.869 --> 43:02.913
and return the world to how it was before.

43:05.457 --> 43:06.542
I will live.

43:10.671 --> 43:11.714
To do that,

43:13.007 --> 43:14.300
I must go to the Beach.

43:40.701 --> 43:42.578
You really don't know
how to ride a bicycle?

43:43.370 --> 43:44.997
I never learned how to ride one.

43:45.080 --> 43:47.082
Even though you're so athletic?

43:51.295 --> 43:52.546
But this feels nice.

46:10.893 --> 46:14.271
Subtitle translation by: Qianni Lu
